Framework: Pydantic v2 (BaseModel, Field, computed_field, field_validator), stdlib enum.Enum / enum.IntEnum, datetime, typing.Annotated.
Design principle: PURE DATA HOLDERS. Only exceptions: Flight.is_delayed (read-only computed_field) and the UTC-normalization field_validators (input normalization, not business logic).

--- Enums ---
AircraftType(str, Enum): NARROW_BODY, WIDE_BODY
FlightStatus(str, Enum): SCHEDULED, IN_AIR, LANDED, AT_GATE, READY_FOR_PUSHBACK, DEPARTED, CANCELLED
GateStatus(str, Enum): OPEN, OCCUPIED, UNAVAILABLE
CrewRole(str, Enum): BAGGAGE, PUSHBACK, CLEANING
DisruptionType(str, Enum): WEATHER, TECH_ISSUE, CREW_SHORTAGE
DisruptionSeverity(IntEnum): LEVEL_1=1 (minor/localized) ... LEVEL_5=5 (critical system-wide halt)

--- Shared validation helper ---
_coerce_utc(value): module-level function in models.py. Normalizes any datetime/str input to timezone-aware UTC (naive -> tagged UTC, aware -> converted to UTC). Used via field_validator(mode="before") on all datetime fields.

--- Models ---
Flight(BaseModel):
  flight_id: str, airline: str, aircraft_type: AircraftType
  scheduled_arrival: datetime, scheduled_departure: datetime  (both UTC-normalized via validator)
  actual_arrival: datetime | None = None, actual_departure: datetime | None = None  (both UTC-normalized via validator)
  status: FlightStatus = SCHEDULED
  assigned_gate: str | None = None
  assigned_crew: list[str] = []  (default_factory)
  turnaround_time: int  (Field(gt=0), required)
  is_delayed: bool  -- computed_field, read-only, True if actual_arrival > scheduled_arrival OR actual_departure > scheduled_departure

CrewMember(BaseModel):
  crew_id: str, role: CrewRole, available: bool (required)
  assigned_flight: str | None = None
  shift_minutes_remaining: int  (Field(ge=0), required)

Gate(BaseModel):
  gate_id: str, supports_wide_body: bool
  gate_status: GateStatus = OPEN
  assigned_flight: str | None = None

DisruptionEvent(BaseModel):
  event_id: str, disruption_type: DisruptionType
  trigger_time: datetime  (UTC-normalized via validator)
  severity: DisruptionSeverity
  disruption_description: str
  affected_flights: list[str] = []  (default_factory)
  resolved: bool = False

Conflict(BaseModel):
  conflict_id: str, agent_id: str, conflict_description: str
  resolved: bool = False
  affected_flights: list[str] = []  (default_factory)

DecisionLogEntry(BaseModel):
  tick: int (Field(ge=0), required), agent_id: str
  action: str  # free-text label, e.g. "gate_assignment", "conflict_raised", "conflict_resolved", "crew_reassigned"; deliberately plain str not enum since action set may grow
  detail: str  # human-readable sentence for the reasoning trace UI
  affected_flights: list[str] = []  (default_factory)

AirportStatus(BaseModel):
  current_tick: int = 0  (Field(ge=0))
  flights: dict[str, Flight] = {}  (default_factory)
  crew: dict[str, CrewMember] = {}  (default_factory)
  gates: dict[str, Gate] = {}  (default_factory)
  open_disruptions: list[DisruptionEvent] = []  (default_factory)
  open_conflicts: list[Conflict] = []  (default_factory)
  decision_log: list[DecisionLogEntry] = []  (default_factory)

